From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:14:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246:
 Bluetooth is a WCN3991
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stock's qcom,wcn3990 is the compatible Qualcomm's btpower gives every
WCN39xx, so it does not name the chip. hci_qca under qcom,wcn3990-bt
read a 15-byte version reply where a WCN3990's is 14 bytes. Of the
WCN39xx chips hci_qca knows, btqca expects 15 bytes only from the
WCN3991.

hci_qca sets loads on the radio's rails but no voltage, so they ran at
the bottom of their windows: vddrf at 1.15 V and vddxo at 1.62 V. The
stock Bluetooth and WLAN drivers ask for 1.304 V and 1.7 to 1.9 V, and
both rails feed only the WCN3991. Raise the floors to 1.304 V and
1.8 V.

To be folded into the SM6450 DT / board DT once it has probed on the device.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts    | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
index 178c169ee..a8105d55d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ pm6450_l13: ldo13 {
 		};
 
 		pm6450_l14: ldo14 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1150000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1304000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1304000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
@@ -217,7 +217,7 @@ pm6150l_s8: smps8 {
 		};
 
 		pm6150l_l1: ldo1 {
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1620000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1980000>;
 		};
 
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@ &uart11 {
 	status = "okay";
 
 	bluetooth {
-		compatible = "qcom,wcn3990-bt";
+		compatible = "qcom,wcn3991-bt";
 
 		vddio-supply = <&pm6450_l22>;
 		vddxo-supply = <&pm6150l_l1>;
